---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";

const T = {
  name: brand.name,
  legal: brand.legalName,
  year: new Date().getFullYear(),
  docVersion: "0.9.0-draft",
  effectiveOn: "TBD — pending Australian legal review",
};
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${brand.name} handles your data.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="pwy-page pwy-legal" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div class="pwy-shell">
      <header class="pwy-legal__head">
        <p class="pwy-kicker">The record / privacy</p>
        <h1 id="privacy-heading">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="pwy-legal__lead">
          {brand.copy.privacyLead} This is the plain-language preview; the formal policy is being finalised
          with Australian legal review.
        </p>
        <p class="pwy-legal__status"><strong>Draft v{T.docVersion}</strong> · {T.effectiveOn}</p>
      </header>

      <h2>Plain-language summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>We collect only what you give us.</strong> Your email, your name, your chapter, your
          birthday (if you give it), your postal address (if you opt in), and the confirmed facts you
          choose to share.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We do not enrich your record from public sources without asking.</strong> AI may propose
          candidate facts (e.g. from inbound email), but candidate facts are stored separately and require
          your confirmation before they are used.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We do not sell your data.</strong> We share it only with named providers when needed
          to deliver the service. Resend and Cloudflare support the current waitlist launch; Stripe is
          not active and no payment is collected.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We do not use your data to train general AI models.</strong> Member data is used to
          run {brand.name}; it is not exported for model training.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We do not infer sensitive personal categories</strong> for personalisation (health,
          political affiliation, religion, sexuality, etc.).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>You can ask us to forget any of it.</strong> Account deletion stops future personalisation
          and triggers the data-removal workflow.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we keep</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address (to write to you)</li>
        <li>Your first name and any preferred name you give us</li>
        <li>Your chapter or metro area, if you give it (so chapter letters are accurate)</li>
        <li>Your birthday, if you give it (so a card can be sent on the right day)</li>
        <li>Your postal address, if you opt in to physical mail (so we can post to you)</li>
        <li>Confirmed facts you choose to share, plus your do-not-mention list</li>
        <li>Membership record (tier, state, joined date, tenure)</li>
        <li>Correspondence history (sent and received, with content for audit)</li>
        <li>
          Required financial records (kept for the minimum period required by law, then removed)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not enrich your record from public sources without asking.</li>
        <li>
          We do not sell your data. We do not share it with third parties except as required to
          deliver the service.
        </li>
        <li>We do not use your data to train general AI models.</li>
        <li>We do not infer sensitive personal categories for personalisation.</li>
        <li>We do not invent facts about you.</li>
        <li>We do not claim fictional characters, locations, or partnerships as real.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your controls</h2>
      <p>
        In the member portal you can see exactly what we remember about you, edit or remove any
        fact, mark any fact as "do not mention", export a copy of your data, and request account
        deletion. You can ask us to forget any of it at any time. The operator can also action this
        on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Provider relationships</h2>
      <p>The third parties we share data with, and the reason:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Resend</strong> — to send and receive email. Resend receives your email address and
          the content of correspondence. Resend is bound by its own privacy policy and data processing
          terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — to host the application, store data in D1 and R2, and serve traffic.
          Cloudflare is bound by its own privacy policy and data processing terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stripe</strong> — planned for payment processing only when billing is enabled. Stripe
          is currently disabled; the waitlist collects no payment method or billing history.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        When you ask to be forgotten, we stop future personalisation and remove your personal data
        subject to legitimate retention requirements (for example, financial records we are required
        to keep for a number of years).
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Australian Privacy Principles and applicable law, you have the right to: (a) request
        access to the personal information we hold about you; (b) request correction of inaccurate
        information; (c) request deletion of your information; (d) make a complaint. To exercise any
        of these rights, contact us via the
        <a href="/waiting-list/">waiting list</a> or by replying to any
        {brand.name} email.
      </p>

      <h2>Status</h2>
      <p class="pwy-legal__version">
        Version: {T.docVersion} · Effective: {T.effectiveOn}<br />
        © {T.year}
        {T.legal}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pwy-page {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pwy-legal {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem) 0 5rem;
  }
  .pwy-legal__head {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .pwy-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font: 600 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .pwy-legal h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5.8rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .pwy-legal__lead {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.8vw, 1.35rem);
  }
  .pwy-legal__status {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 0.75rem/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .pwy-legal > .pwy-shell > h2 {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  .pwy-legal h2 {
    font: 400 clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem)/1 var(--font-serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .pwy-legal h3 {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    font: 400 1.4rem/1.1 var(--font-serif);
  }
  .pwy-legal p,
  .pwy-legal li {
    max-width: 48rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .pwy-legal li {
    margin: 0.7rem 0;
  }
  .pwy-legal strong {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .pwy-legal__version {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--fg-faint) !important;
    font: 0.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);
  }
</style>
